-- title:
--   Semilinearity of Drinfeld charts at supersingular points
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a nonzero $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$; let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ for $\{q\ell\}$, with $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity, $\xi$ a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity and $\zeta = \xi^{\ell}$. Let $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ be the intersection of the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$ with the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times$, and let $K$ be the $L$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal, with $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, with uniformiser $\varpi$, and with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion the coefficient image of the $q$-expansion $\mathsf{jq}$ of the $j$-function, and let $X = \mathrm{TwoChartIntegralModel}\,A\,K\,j$ be the pushout of the two affine charts $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the integral closures of $A[j]$ and $A[j^{-1}]$ in $K$. Let $z$ be a point of $X$ whose stalk contains, in its maximal ideal, the germ $\varpi_z$ of the image of $\varpi$ under the structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} A$, let $y$ be a point of the finite chart $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathcal{A}_{\mathrm{fin}} = \mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K\,j$ mapping to $z$, and assume that $y$ is supersingular in the sense that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : \mathcal{A}_{\mathrm{fin}} \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$ the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,q\,\Omega$, i.e. every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero point killed by $q$. Let $W$ be an adically complete discrete valuation domain, $\sigma : A \to W$ a ring homomorphism with $\mathfrak{m}_W = (\sigma\varpi)$, let $u, v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ be units and $f \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ congruent to the Drinfeld form $X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and let $e$ be a ring isomorphism from the $\mathfrak{m}$-adic completion of the stalk of $X$ at $z$ onto $S = W[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma\varpi)v - fu)$ which reads constants correctly: for every $a \in A$, $e$ sends the image in the completion of the germ at $z$ of $a$ to the class of $C(\sigma a)$. Write $\mathrm{germY} : \mathcal{A}_{\mathrm{fin}} \to \mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ for the germ map through the finite chart. The conclusion asserts: for all ring automorphisms $\sigma_L$ of $L$ and $\sigma_A$ of $A$ with $\sigma_L$ restricting to $\sigma_A$ along $A \to L$ and $\sigma_A \equiv \mathrm{id} \pmod{\mathfrak{m}_A}$, and every ring automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ acting on Laurent series by applying $\sigma_L$ to coefficients, such that $\tau$ and $\tau^{-1}$ preserve $\mathcal{A}_{\mathrm{fin}}$ and $\tau(a) - a \in y$ for all $a \in \mathcal{A}_{\mathrm{fin}}$, there exist a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$ and a ring automorphism $\sigma_W$ of $W$ such that $\theta$ intertwines $e \circ \mathrm{germY}$ with the restriction of $\tau$ to $\mathcal{A}_{\mathrm{fin}}$, $\sigma_W \circ \sigma = \sigma \circ \sigma_A$, $\sigma_W(w) - w \in \mathfrak{m}_W$ for all $w \in W$, and $\theta$ acts on the classes of constants $C(w)$ by $\sigma_W$.
--
--   This transports an automorphism of the $j$-finite chart algebra that fixes a supersingular point and reduces to the identity there into a $\sigma_W$-semilinear automorphism of the Drinfeld local chart $W[[X_0,X_1]]/(\sigma\varpi\,v - fu)$ at that point, in the auxiliary level structure with $H_1$ cutting out congruence to $1$ modulo $q$ and modulo $\ell$. It is used in the analysis of the action of inertia on the Drinfeld chart, where the linear part of the induced automorphism is computed.
